[{:db/id "q-351003/field-1/b405c37a8febc096e8401f6556dbed88bd549a6a16a7301ef3a001752b742d97" :answer/id #uuid "f0b128cb-762b-5ac3-9e2e-ab6bd5e30399" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3t^4+10t^2+12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351003/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d42913a8-486c-5cdb-b6ff-a9765aa155fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351003/field-1/b405c37a8febc096e8401f6556dbed88bd549a6a16a7301ef3a001752b742d97" :answer-field/choices ["q-351003/field-1/b405c37a8febc096e8401f6556dbed88bd549a6a16a7301ef3a001752b742d97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351003" :question/id #uuid "ef5a528e-3d29-5ffb-a668-9fd133c57543" :question/math-academy-id "q-351003" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in $\\text{ft}/{\\text{s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=12{t}^{3}+20t,$ where $t$ is the time in seconds. Find the velocity $v(t)$ (in $\\text{ft/s}$) of the particle at time $t$ given that the particle has velocity $v=25\\,\\text{ft/s}$ when $t=1\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n$v(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (12{t}^{3}+20t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{t}^{4}+10{t}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(1)=25.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25 & =3({1}^{4})+10({1}^{2})+C \\\\ 25 & =13+C \\\\ C & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=3{t}^{4}+10{t}^{2}+12.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-351003/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee2920dc-93e1-5595-a751-62ad5e4f3035"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351003"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351027/field-1/b3063427b0ff89ffe2ddea5abf57fdb2d84e5b29f01c8b9a63dda03e6854085b" :answer/id #uuid "6e2e28b2-dd67-5539-a65d-4d62b7df06e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\cos(t)+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351027/field-1/565659232a3fa97a0ccd0b5407e7f4a307b2e0108e67ce5671ac55c7356a2f4e" :answer/id #uuid "5f611c80-3aed-5021-b1b6-999a77942a65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\cos(t)+10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351027/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1f020414-ee06-5bdc-a0d2-e4713f6d9b12" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351027/field-1/b3063427b0ff89ffe2ddea5abf57fdb2d84e5b29f01c8b9a63dda03e6854085b" :answer-field/choices ["q-351027/field-1/b3063427b0ff89ffe2ddea5abf57fdb2d84e5b29f01c8b9a63dda03e6854085b" "q-351027/field-1/565659232a3fa97a0ccd0b5407e7f4a307b2e0108e67ce5671ac55c7356a2f4e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351027" :question/id #uuid "965499a4-cbc7-5edc-bbf6-55706f2f19ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-351027" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in ${\\text{m /s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t),$ where $t>0$ is the time in seconds. Find the velocity $v(t)$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of the particle at time $t$ given that the particle has velocity $v=10\\,\\text{m /s}$ when $t=\\pi \\,\\text{s}.$\n\n$v(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(\\pi )=10.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+C \\\\ 10 & =-6(-1)+C \\\\ 10 & =6+C \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-351027/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f20159e8-8f86-5bf8-b87e-3eb990b819f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351027"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351051/field-1/311181592c4a8734d2ff1bd5a96dc4ba85394768c842512eca8aaa3e2b122b71" :answer/id #uuid "ec671c1e-8977-579d-900b-a5adce9b2587" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{t}-3t+10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351051/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c177ed9b-7caf-5cbe-8bfa-16833e78f3f8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351051/field-1/311181592c4a8734d2ff1bd5a96dc4ba85394768c842512eca8aaa3e2b122b71" :answer-field/choices ["q-351051/field-1/311181592c4a8734d2ff1bd5a96dc4ba85394768c842512eca8aaa3e2b122b71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351051" :question/id #uuid "8b1822ff-b3b6-5a2a-882b-65b7f52390da" :question/math-academy-id "q-351051" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration, measured in ${\\text{ft/s}}^{2},$ given by the function $a(t)=\\frac{6}{{t}^{2}}-3,$ where $t>0$ is the time in seconds. Find the velocity $v(t)$ (in $\\text{ft/s}$) of the particle at time $t$ given that the particle has velocity $v=1\\,\\text{ft/s}$ when $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$\n\n$v(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{6}{{t}^{2}}-3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{6}{{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+\\int (-3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{t}-3t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(2)=1.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-\\frac{6}{2}-3(2)+C \\\\ 1 & =-9+C \\\\ C & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)=-\\frac{6}{t}-3t+10.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-351051/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f20159e8-8f86-5bf8-b87e-3eb990b819f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351051"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
